menu "Chamber Screen"

    config CS_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default "changeme"
        help
            Network the controller joins for the web UI and OTA updates.

    config CS_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password"
        default "changeme"

    config CS_WIFI_MAX_RETRY
        int "WiFi connect retries before giving up"
        default 8
        help
            After this many failures the controller carries on without a
            network. Local control must never depend on the cloud, so this
            is not fatal.

    config CS_HOSTNAME
        string "Hostname / mDNS name"
        default "fridge"

    config CS_WEBUI_ENABLE
        bool "Enable web UI, live log and OTA upload"
        default y
        help
            Serves a status page with a live log tail and accepts firmware
            uploads. Development convenience: there is NO authentication,
            so keep this off any network you do not trust.

    config CS_NETLOG_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "In-memory log ring buffer (bytes)"
        default 6144
        depends on CS_WEBUI_ENABLE
        help
            Statically allocated, so it comes straight out of internal DRAM -
            which WiFi, BLE and TLS have largely spoken for already. 12 KB
            here was enough to overflow dram0_0_seg once LVGL was linked in.
            6 KB still holds a useful tail; the browser keeps the history.

endmenu
